  message: "A SECOND INSTANCE OF THE SAME PATTERN, found in the same sweep: packages/hypergumbo-lang-extended1/tests/test_llvm_ir.py::TestAnalyzeLlvmIr::test_cross_file_call_resolution also fails locally at 4c82fe0131, in isolation, while PR #639's CI passed at that commit. Different package, different language, same local-red/CI-green shape. Two independent instances make 'flaky test' a weaker explanation than 'the local environment differs from CI in something both tests depend on' -- and cross-FILE call resolution is, like the namespace-import case, a question about which of several same-named candidates wins, which is exactly where enumeration order decides. Worth checking whether both resolve through the same ordering-sensitive code path before treating them as two bugs. Neither was caused by INV-kanuk's catalogue change: that diff touches only go.yaml, two go overlays and two hypergumbo-core test files, none of which test_llvm_ir.py or test_js_ts.py imports."  # 36f8
